GPIO_TC_004	gp0_gpio_8 Write-Read 0xFFFFFFFF	Write 0xFFFFFFFF to gp0_gpio_8 and read back. Only writable bits (WRITE_MASK=0x003F0000) should be set. RO/WO fields unaffected.	gpio_reg_wr_rd_test	program.c, test_define.c	GPIO	MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8	0xA001A000 + 0x0	gp0_gpio_8	0x0	32	pedge_intr_en, nedge_intr_en, level_sel, io_ctrl, dout	17, 18, 19, 20, 21	RW, RW, RW, RW2, RW2	0x00100000	hreset_n	1. Reset released. 2. AHB clock running.	1. Write 0xFFFFFFFF to MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8. 2. Read back register. 3. Apply READ_MASK (0x003E0002) to compare. Expected readable writable bits: pedge_intr_en=1, nedge_intr_en=1, level_sel=1, io_ctrl=1, dout=1.	Read value masked with 0x003F0003 = 0x003E0002 (readable writable bits set). RO fields reflect HW state. WO field (intr_clr) reads 0.	write, read	Write-Read Verification	High	Not Run	Pattern 0xFFFFFFFF. WRITE_MASK=0x003F0000. Bits[31:22] and [15:2] are reserved.
