GPIO_TC_013	gp0_gpio_8 RO Field Verification - data_in	Verify data_in[0] field in gp0_gpio_8 is read-only. Write should not change the field value.	gpio_reg_wr_rd_test	program.c, test_define.c	GPIO	MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8	0xA001A000 + 0x0	gp0_gpio_8	0x0	32	data_in	0	RO	0	hreset_n	1. Reset released. 2. AHB clock running.	1. Read gp0_gpio_8 and note data_in[0] value. 2. Write 0x00000001 to gp0_gpio_8. 3. Read back gp0_gpio_8. 4. Verify data_in[0] is unchanged (reflects HW pin state, not written value).	data_in[0] value unchanged after write. RO field is not writable.	read, write, read	RO Field Verification	Medium	Not Run	data_in is a hardware-driven read-only field reflecting GPIO pin level.
GPIO_TC_014	gp0_gpio_8 RO Field Verification - intr_raw_sts	Verify intr_raw_sts[1] field in gp0_gpio_8 is read-only. Write should not change the field value.	gpio_reg_wr_rd_test	program.c, test_define.c	GPIO	MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8	0xA001A000 + 0x0	gp0_gpio_8	0x0	32	intr_raw_sts	1	RO	0	hreset_n	1. Reset released. 2. AHB clock running.	1. Read gp0_gpio_8 and note intr_raw_sts[1] value. 2. Write 0x00000002 to gp0_gpio_8. 3. Read back gp0_gpio_8. 4. Verify intr_raw_sts[1] is unchanged.	intr_raw_sts[1] value unchanged after write. RO field is not writable.	read, write, read	RO Field Verification	Medium	Not Run	intr_raw_sts reflects latched raw interrupt status.
GPIO_TC_015	gp0_gpio_8 WO Field Verification - intr_clr	Verify intr_clr[16] field in gp0_gpio_8 is write-only. Read should return 0.	gpio_reg_wr_rd_test	program.c, test_define.c	GPIO	MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8	0xA001A000 + 0x0	gp0_gpio_8	0x0	32	intr_clr	16	WO	0	hreset_n	1. Reset released. 2. AHB clock running.	1. Write 0x00010000 to gp0_gpio_8 (set intr_clr[16]=1). 2. Read back gp0_gpio_8. 3. Verify bit[16] reads as 0 (WO field).	Bit[16] (intr_clr) reads 0 after write. WO field always reads 0.	write, read	WO Field Verification	Medium	Not Run	Writing 1 to intr_clr clears the interrupt raw status. Writing 0 has no change.
GPIO_TC_016	gp0_gpio_8 RW Field Verification - pedge_intr_en	Verify pedge_intr_en[17] field in gp0_gpio_8 is read-write. Write 1 then read back should return 1.	gpio_reg_wr_rd_test	program.c, test_define.c	GPIO	MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8	0xA001A000 + 0x0	gp0_gpio_8	0x0	32	pedge_intr_en	17	RW	0	hreset_n	1. Reset released. 2. AHB clock running.	1. Write 0x00020000 to gp0_gpio_8 (set pedge_intr_en[17]=1). 2. Read back gp0_gpio_8. 3. Verify bit[17]=1. 4. Write 0x00000000 to clear. 5. Read back and verify bit[17]=0.	pedge_intr_en[17] toggles between 1 and 0 as written. RW field is fully writable and readable.	write, read	RW Field Verification	Medium	Not Run	Pos-edge interrupt enable. 1=Enable interrupt on rising edge detection.
GPIO_TC_017	gp0_gpio_8 RW2 Field Verification - io_ctrl	Verify io_ctrl[20] field in gp0_gpio_8 is RW2 type. Default=1 (input mode). Write 0 to set output mode, read back should reflect HW state.	gpio_reg_wr_rd_test	program.c, test_define.c	GPIO	MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8	0xA001A000 + 0x0	gp0_gpio_8	0x0	32	io_ctrl	20	RW2	1	hreset_n	1. Reset released. 2. AHB clock running.	1. Read gp0_gpio_8 and verify io_ctrl[20]=1 (default input mode). 2. Write 0x00000000 to gp0_gpio_8 (clear io_ctrl[20]=0, output mode). 3. Read back and verify io_ctrl[20] reflects HW state.	io_ctrl[20] default=1 (input mode). After write 0, io_ctrl[20] reflects output mode. RW2 type: read returns HW-driven value.	read, write, read	RW2 Field Verification	Medium	Not Run	RW2: Read-write type-2. Read returns HW-driven value. 0=Output mode, 1=Input mode.
GPIO_TC_018	gp0_gpio_8 RW2 Field Verification - dout	Verify dout[21] field in gp0_gpio_8 is RW2 type. Default=0. Write 1 to set output data, read back should reflect HW state.	gpio_reg_wr_rd_test	program.c, test_define.c	GPIO	MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8	0xA001A000 + 0x0	gp0_gpio_8	0x0	32	dout	21	RW2	0	hreset_n	1. Reset released. 2. AHB clock running.	1. Read gp0_gpio_8 and verify dout[21]=0 (default). 2. Set io_ctrl[20]=0 (output mode). 3. Write 0x00200000 to gp0_gpio_8 (set dout[21]=1). 4. Read back and verify dout[21] reflects HW state.	dout[21] default=0. After write 1, dout[21] reflects output data value. RW2 type: read returns HW-driven value.	read, write, read	RW2 Field Verification	Medium	Not Run	RW2: dout value written to GPIO pin in output mode.
